<p style="color:#ccc;margin:0;line-height:1.75;font-size:.95rem;">A growth strategy is the executive-level plan that defines how a B2B company will increase revenue -- specifying the growth levers (new customer acquisition, expansion revenue, new markets, new products), the investment required, and the milestones that indicate the strategy is working. For companies at $1M to $20M ARR, the highest-leverage growth strategies combine ICP discipline, repeatable demand generation, and a sales motion that converts marketing pipeline at predictable rates -- rather than relying on founder relationships and referrals that cannot scale.</p>
</div>

